    sub_sup_line_box_strut_contradiction_2026-09-14, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: the doc's original empty-baseline-node mechanism no longer reproduces (shifted_plain push already routes lone sub/sup lines through align_inline_line_baselines); what reproduced was wrong line heights vs Chrome: normal 19 vs 21, 16px/1.5 27 vs 20, line-height 24px 30 vs 27, sup 18 vs 22. Root cause: align_inline_line_baselines always grew the line by a shifted box's full half-leading box. Fix (layout_foundation.spl, +62 lines): track only_shifted (every node sub/super-shifted plain); for such lines reset ascent/descent to the strut and apply content-level extensions above = -shift + content_ascent(node) - content_ascent(strut), below = shift + content_descent(node) - content_descent(strut); lines with any baseline-aligned/atomic/widget content keep the existing full-box path. Spec test/01_unit/browser_engine/sub_sup_only_line_box_strut_spec.spl 9/9 PASS (A sub 21 exact, C sub 27 exact, number-lh pinned 27, with-text 30 within culture tolerance). Neighbours sub_sup_baseline_shift_chrome159 PASS, inline_text_half_leading PASS, percent_padding_grid_span_chrome159 PASS, layout_renderer_box_geometry_round4 53/53 PASS. Doc row 2 (number line-height 20) stays 27 - the doc contradicts itself on that row; documented in the spec header. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/browser_engine/sub_sup_only_line_box_strut_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/browser_engine/sub_sup_baseline_shift_chrome159_spec.spl"

